Destiny is built with Destiny

The host compiler (`HOST_DC`) is now a released Destiny compiler: a destiny64
package from Destiny-Org/host-compilers, installed with
`ci/host_compiler.sh destiny-<version>`. No upstream D compiler is used to
build Destiny, its libraries or tools.

$(UL
$(LI Without `HOST_DC`, the build uses `destiny` from `PATH`.)
$(LI With a Destiny host, the Makefiles build `build.d`, `run.d` and the
druntime test extractor with `-revert=safedefault`.)
$(LI CI runs on Linux only, the one platform destiny64 is packaged for.)
)
